          "path": "_m/g/c/u/g/tarbolton-wp/tarbolton-motte-from-the-baile.jpg",
          "filename": "Tarbolton Motte From The Bailey - geograph.org.uk - 1304437.jpg",
          "caption": "Tarbolton Motte From The Bailey The 12th century Motte at Tarbolton was surrounded on 3 sides by a Bailey.  In this view, the sloping edge of the Motte is seen from the flat platform that was the Bailey.  The Motte was the site of a wooden house or tower, which would be the home of the local lord.  The Bailey was a surrounding base court containing the necessary services, such as stables, kitchens and workshops.  Tarbolton Bailey would have been protected by a timber fence, combined with the naturally steep slope on 3 sides.  (Source:  The Castles of South-West Scotland\", by Mike Salter)",
          "alt": "Tarbolton Motte From The Bailey The 12th century Motte at Tarbolton was surrounded on 3 sides by a Bailey.  In this view, the sloping edge of the Motte is seen from the flat platform that was the Bailey.  The Motte was the site of a wooden house or tower, which would be the home of the local lord.  The Bailey was a surrounding base court containing the necessary services, such as stables, kitchens and workshops.  Tarbolton Bailey would have been protected by a timber fence, combined with the naturally steep slope on 3 sides.  (Source:  The Castles of South-West Scotland\", by Mike Salter)",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 426,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Mary and Angus Hogg",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tarbolton_Motte_From_The_Bailey_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1304437.jpg",
